  "chapter": 685,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 65 Chapter 685\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 3876, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring\n        comparison of prices charged by energy services companies\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require each billing statement for an ESCO customer to\ninclude a side-by-side comparison of the price charged by the  ESCO  and\nthe  charges the customer would have paid if they were a customer of the\nincumbent utility, along with an itemized list of any additional charges\nfor products provided by the  ESCO.  It  would  also  require  ESCOs  to\nprovide  an annual statement to customers comparing the price charged by\nthe ESCO with the price the customer would have paid  to  the  incumbent\nutility for the prior twelve months.\n \n  I  fully  support  empowering ESCO customers and promoting information\ntransparency through providing on-bill price  comparisons  of  ESCO  and\nincumbent  utility charges. Presenting the comparison on the bill itself\nwould provide ESCO customers with an  efficient,  prompt,  and  one-stop\nmeans  to  see  and check the different prices. However, changes to this\nbill were necessary to address technical  issues  and  to  ensure  costs\nassociated with implementing this bill were not passed on to customers.\n \n  I reached an agreement with the legislature to enact these changes. On\nthe basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
